      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 1. The poet begins with a salutation to Brahman, the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "<i>Supreme Ens</i>, which is one of the three modes prescribed for the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "opening of a poem by Sanskṛt writers on Poetics, <i>viz.</i> आशीर्नम-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "स्क्रिया वस्तुनिर्देशो वापि तन्मुखम्[*]—A blessing (to be conferred on the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "readers ), a salutation ( to the favourite Deity ) and an indica-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "tion of the subject matter are the three prescribed forms of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "introduction to a poem. It is also usual with Sanskrit writers",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "to have what is technically called <i>Mangalàcharana</i>. This is done",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "either directly by an appeal to the favourite deity itself or to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "some of its attributes, or by the use of some such word as अथ",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "and the like. The efficacy of this <i>mangala</i> is emphasised by all",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "kinds of writers; see Patan. quoted in the com.",
          "end": "line"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "The Vedântic character of the sl. the student will easily mark.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "दिक्काल—space and time; अवच्छिन्न is lit. what is cut off from all",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "sides, is contained in another, is measured: अनवच्छिन्न means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "what is unmeasured; hence undefined, unconditioned. आदि",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "refers to qualities ( <i>gunas</i> ) such as धर्म, अधर्म &c., as well as to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "कार्यs ( effects ) &c. न विद्यते अन्तः यस्य तदनन्तं infinite. चिन्मात्रमूर्ति—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "चिन्मात्र pure intelligence or knowledge. A Karm. of the मयूरव्यंस-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "कादि class. ॰मूर्तिः whose form is pure intelligence. दिक्का॰-ये—A",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "<i>Tripada</i> Karm. This is the best way of taking the Comp. The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "attributes of Brahma, here expressed, are summed up in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "<i>Mahâva`kya</i>—‘सत्यं ज्ञानमनन्तं ब्रह्म’ of the Taittirîya Upanishad.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "Another way is to analyse the Comp. as a Bah. with मूर्ति as the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "second member with all that precedes as its attributive member,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "itself being a Comp. of three adjectives. मूर्ति is derived from",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 20,
          "text": "मूच्छ्र् 1. P. to settle into a solid form + क्तिन्, and literally means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 21,
          "text": "what is visible to the senses; hence secondarily what is per-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 22,
          "text": "ceptible by the mind. TheDat. sing, of neu. adj s ending in इ is",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
